From 036147c8c123a8c095f44fcfd8079dbea8e9f68e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: faycal <faycalelhandi9@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 6 Nov 2026 20:55:23 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 06/35] feat(hybrid): Kyty's renderer runs Astro Bot inside
 AstroBot.exe (milestone 2)

- Memory: AnyPS5's guest arena hands Kyty placeholder ranges (the PS5
  system-managed area 0x200000000-0x7ffff0000, the driver memory range
  around 0x0fe0000000 and a 64 GiB window); Kyty adopts them as owned free
  space (Memory::AdoptHostPlaceholders) instead of scanning the process,
  and leaves them to the host at teardown. The game's direct and flexible
  memory calls (17 libkernel NIDs, also those of the bundled guest libc)
  are exported for AnyPS5's libkernel to forward.
- Write tracking: the bridge installs Kyty's guest access fault handler as
  a first-chance handler (kyty_emulator does it in the runtime linker).
- Lazy start publishes the exports only after the renderer is up, so other
  game threads wait in the trap instead of calling an uninitialized Kyty.
- tools/hybrid/build_kyty_gpu.py also recompiles the hybrid-changed Kyty
  sources (kernel/memory.cpp) and links them in place of the emulator's.

AstroBot.exe (AnyPS5 relinked) with Build\RunHybrid: the title screen
renders correctly at 51-60 fps (run-20261106-205252).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
